# Running mlface with PyTorch MPS (Option A) on Apple Silicon

This branch (`option-a-mps`) implements Option A: **Face Detection and Recognition using PyTorch with MPS (Metal Performance Shaders) acceleration**.

---

## Standard Installation (Homebrew Service)

The preferred way to run this on macOS is as a local Homebrew service. This moves the execution off external mounts to the local SSD for better performance.

1. **Install files and setup Virtual Environment**:
   ```bash
   sudo make install
   ```
   This installs everything to `/usr/local/lib/mlface/`.

2. **Configure and start the Homebrew service**:
   ```bash
   make brew-setup
   ```

3. **Manage the service**:
   ```bash
   brew services list
   brew services restart mlface
   tail -f /usr/local/var/log/mlface.log
   ```

## Manual Prerequisites & Installation

1. **Install System Dependencies** using [Homebrew](https://brew.sh/):
   ```bash
   brew install cmake boost
   ```

2. **Set up a Virtual Environment**:
   ```bash
   python3 -m venv venv
   source venv/bin/activate
   ```

3. **Install Requirements**:
   ```bash
   pip install --upgrade pip
   pip install -r requirements_mps.txt
   ```

## Running the Service

Start the GPU-accelerated face recognition server:
```bash
python3 mlface_mps.py -d ./known_faces
```

This runs the websocket service on port `4785`, utilizing your M2's GPU via Metal Performance Shaders for both detection (MTCNN) and embedding extraction (FaceNet / VGGface2).
